;; README.slatl — Motoi Scheme Reference · error-cards · BOOT RECORD
;;
;; The boot record for the error-cards folder-book, per spec/BOOK-LAYOUT.slat.
;; First file any reader (human, LLM, Rosetta) opens here. It briefs a cold
;; reader on what this shelf is, when to read it, and what is inside, and carries
;; the ordered nav that renders to a Markdown table of contents. Programs read
;; MANIFEST.slat for structure; this file is the human+LLM landing page.
(dialect :applies ("motoi") :note "Boot record for the Motoi error-cards catalogue.")

(boot-record
  :book-title "Motoi Scheme — Error Cards"
  :book-kind  "error-card-catalogue"
  :book-slug  "motoi-error-cards"
  :boot-into  "SCHEMA.slat"
  :card-count 10
  :for        ("human-reader" "motoi-model" "llm-training" "llm-inference"
               "language-engineer" "sre" "returning-collaborator"
               "rosetta-render-target")
  :training-eligible #t
  :confidentiality "public"

  :what-this-is
  "This folder is the ERROR-CARD CATALOGUE — one card per KIND of failure Motoi
   can produce, keyed to the error census. Where broken-examples/ teaches ONE
   program that will not run and its fix, an error card teaches ONE COORDINATE of
   the census: the stable normalized-key that `normalizeError`
   (lib/system/verb-stats.js) maps a thrown thing to, the coordinate
   `stats/error-count-of` counts against. It is the WRONG SINK made legible.
   Every card is grounded in ACTUAL runtime behaviour — each :trigger-code was
   run through `./bin/motoi run` and reproduces its :observed-output verbatim.
   No brochure of what a Scheme 'should' do; only what Motoi HONESTLY does."

  :when-to-read
  "Read a card when the census surfaces a key and you need to know what that
   wrong MEANS — how to recognize it at a verb, how to detect it in code, and
   what the honest fix is. Read the whole shelf when you are doing language or
   module development and want the true shape of Motoi's error surface: the clean
   language errors, the leaky-host collisions, the two BLIND SPOTS (silent
   non-errors and pre-eval reader/expand errors) the census cannot see, and the
   reserved roster keys Motoi does not yet throw. If you are the Motoi model
   reading your own runtime, this is your RAG index on throw: retrieve by key,
   steer away on suggest."

  :whats-inside
  "A SCHEMA (the card format), a MANIFEST (the machine index + roster-coverage
   ledger), nine hand-authored cards, and scripts/mint-error-cards.mjs — the
   system for the PRODUCTION OF MORE. The nine cards cover the whole honest
   surface: three clean language errors (unbound-symbol, fuel-exhausted, and the
   two escaped-user-condition classes), the leaky-host collision sink
   (not-a-procedure), the normalizer floor (misc-uncategorized), and three cards
   naming what the census CANNOT count — silent non-errors, reader/expand-time
   errors, and the reserved-but-never-thrown roster keys."

  :not-here
  "Only the ERROR SURFACE lives here. Individual won't-run programs and their
   fixes live in ../broken-examples/. The verb definitions live in the numbered
   reference chapters. The introspection verbs that OBSERVE these keys at runtime
   (stats/error-counts, stats/error-count-of, stats/error-summary,
   stats/error-novel) are documented in ../00b-introspection.slat. The census
   ENGINE is lib/system/verb-stats.js."

  ;; ─── How a card is born (the production system) ──────────────
  :production
  "New cards arrive two ways. (1) HAND-AUTHORED for instructive keys — the nine
   here. (2) MINTED: scripts/mint-error-cards.mjs reads the live census
   (~/.motoi/stats.slat, override MOTOI_STATS_PATH) + the static family roster in
   verb-stats.js, cross-references the cards that already exist, and scaffolds a
   :status \"provisional\" stub for any key with no card yet. A human (or the
   model) then fills the stub's :meaning/:fix-shape/:lesson and flips it to
   :status \"real\". The census surfaces a new wrong; the mint makes a place to
   teach it; a person authors the teaching. Run: `node scripts/mint-error-cards.mjs`."

  ;; ─── The honesty rule (hard) ─────────────────────────────────
  :honesty-rule
  "Every :trigger-code MUST actually produce its :observed-output, verified via
   `echo '<trigger-code>' | ./bin/motoi run /dev/stdin`, and :normalizes-to MUST
   be the key the live census actually records. No aspirational output. No
   fabricated key. When a roster family exists in the normalizer but Motoi does
   not throw it, the card says so with :census-status \"roster-only-not-observed\"."

  :nav
  (
   (:n "0"  :title "Card format (schema)"        :file "SCHEMA.slat"                 :purpose "the required + optional fields of an error card, filename rule, honesty rule")
   (:n "1"  :title "unbound-symbol"              :file "unbound-symbol.slatl"        :purpose "counted-real — a name with no binding, the common clean error")
   (:n "2"  :title "not-a-procedure"             :file "not-a-procedure.slatl"       :purpose "counted-via-collision — applying a non-procedure + the leaky-host sink")
   (:n "3"  :title "fuel-exhausted"              :file "fuel-exhausted.slatl"        :purpose "counted-real — the uncatchable budget error (guard cannot run)")
   (:n "4"  :title "class:ErrorObject"           :file "class-ErrorObject.slatl"     :purpose "counted-real — an escaped (error \"...\" ...) R7RS error object")
   (:n "5"  :title "class:RaisedValue"           :file "class-RaisedValue.slatl"     :purpose "counted-real — an escaped (raise obj) control signal")
   (:n "6"  :title "class:TypeError"             :file "class-TypeError.slatl"       :purpose "counted-real — the non-colliding leaky-host TypeError (sibling of not-a-procedure)")
   (:n "7"  :title "misc-uncategorized"          :file "misc-uncategorized.slatl"    :purpose "counted-real — the normalizer floor, real errors that match no family")
   (:n "8"  :title "silent-non-errors"           :file "silent-non-errors.slatl"     :purpose "uncounted — the blind spot: wrong value, nothing thrown")
   (:n "9"  :title "reader-time + expand-time"   :file "expand-and-reader-time.slatl" :purpose "uncounted — real errors before the eval boundary")
   (:n "10" :title "roster keys not yet observed" :file "roster-not-observed.slatl"  :purpose "roster-only — reserved keys Motoi never throws today")
  ))
